    "synopsis": {
        "native": "Alors que la presse doit faire face aux grands bouleversements que repr\u00e9sentent l\u2019arriv\u00e9e des blogs, tweets et autres r\u00e9volutions du web, ce film propose une plong\u00e9e au coeur du travail des journalistes du service politique du Monde, lors de la campagne \u00e9lectorale de 2012. Dans la r\u00e9daction comme sur le terrain, nous assistons ainsi aux d\u00e9bats qui traversent le grand quotidien du soir. Spectateurs privil\u00e9gi\u00e9s des oppositions et des tensions de la r\u00e9daction, nous partageons aussi l\u2019enthousiasme et les fous rires des journalistes, la fatigue et les doutes, le quotidien du quotidien. Le portrait d\u2019un m\u00e9tier en profonde mutation dans un des titres les plus prestigieux de la presse mondiale, qui s\u2019appr\u00eate \u00e0 f\u00eater ses soixante-dix ans.",
        "english": "While the press media industry grapples with dramatic changes brought about by blogs, twitter, and other internet revolutions, this documentary takes us on a journey into the world of political journalists working for the French newspaper Le Monde during the presidential election campaign in 2012. Following journalists in the field and behind their desks, we are given an insider\u2019s view of the great debates taking place behind the walls of this legendary French news machine. We witness the tensions and antagonisms within the editorial team and share journalists' excitement and fits of laughter, their fatigue and uncertainties\u2014all part of the daily life of a daily newspaper. It is a portrait of a rapidly changing profession set within one of the world\u2019s most prestigious news organizations, which will soon celebrate its 70th anniversary."
    },
